mments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qblr8z/frstpm_completely_useless_80287"},{"short_id":"jf99rj","created_at":"2026-11-24T18:41:24.453-06:00","title":"Can Passcode support be vibecoded for Lobsters?","url":"","score":-4,"flags":5,"comment_count":7,"description":"\u003cp\u003eIt's \u0026lt;the current year\u0026gt; -- could we add passkey support? Here's a prompt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExtend the existing Ruby on Rails \u0026amp; Vanilla JS codebase to provide the minimal necessary user interface , frontend \u0026amp; backend implementations to support webauthn/passkeys.  Support multiple passkeys per user.  Support passkey detection when the user is logged out, so the user credential can be automatically detected without input.   Do not include any third party frameworks, use only vanilla JS and common browser APIs. ensure compatibility with Chromium, Safari and Firefox.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI swear on my PS4 that I wrote this message.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"It's \u003cthe current year\u003e -- could we add passkey support? Here's a prompt. \r\n\r\n\r\n\u003e Extend the existing Ruby on Rails \u0026 Vanilla JS codebase to provide the minimal necessary user interface , frontend \u0026 backend implementations to support webauthn/passkeys.  Support multiple passkeys per user.  Support passkey detection when the user is logged out, so the user credential can be automatically detected without input.   Do not include any third party frameworks, use only vanilla JS and common browser APIs. ensure compatibility with Chromium, Safari and Firefox.\r\n\r\nI swear on my PS4 that I wrote this message.","submitter_user":"tonymet","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","culture","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jf99rj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jf99rj/can_passcode_support_be_vibecoded_for"},{"short_id":"l7fel2","created_at":"2026-11-24T18:02:36.960-06:00","title":"Dutch data protection